thread:
olivia: FYI hitting a weird flake in the sample Android app when the SDK retries a POST with a streaming RequestBody. getting \"java.io.IOException: request body is not repeatable\" on retry.

sam: ugh. is this on Android 13/14 or emulator? which okhttp version?

olivia: Android 14 on Pixel 8, okhttp 4.11.0 in the app. Happens when network hiccups mid-upload and our RetryInterceptor retries automatically.

nina: common cause: RequestBody that streams from a FileDescriptor/InputStream can't be replayed for retries. OkHttp retries expect repeatable bodies unless you buffer them.

raj: do we have a per-request flag to disable automatic retry for non-repeatable bodies? I thought our SDK set callTimeout/retryOnConnectionFailure globally.

olivia: SDK currently uses a global OkHttp client with retryOnConnectionFailure=true and a custom RetryInterceptor that does 3 attempts. didn't consider non-repeatable body case.

sam: quick fixes: 1) make RequestBody repeatable by buffering (Memory or temp file). 2) mark the request so interceptor skips retry. 3) use newRequestBuilder.tag() to attach a boolean and check in interceptor.

nina: example interceptor check we used elsewhere:

```kotlin
class RetryInterceptor: Interceptor {
  override fun intercept(chain: Interceptor.Chain): Response {
    val req = chain.request()
    val skip = req.tag(Boolean::class.java) ?: false
    var attempt = 0
    while (true) {
      try {
        return chain.proceed(req)
      } catch (e: IOException) {
        if (skip || attempt++ >= 2) throw e
      }
    }
  }
}
```

raj: nice. can we detect non-repeatable bodies automatically? maybe check if request.body() is a known repeatable type or has contentLength() >= 0?

nina: contentLength!=-1 is not a guarantee but helps. For streaming bodies length often -1. We can default to skipping retries when contentLength == -1 and log a warning.

olivia: another angle: sample app onboarding doc should call out "if you upload streams, set request.tag(Boolean) to true to disable sdk retry". right now docs assume all bodies are retry-safe.

sam: agree. also add an example showing how to wrap a stream in a BufferedRequestBody that writes to tmp file with .use and deletes after send. mention memory implications.

raj: i'll open a tiny PR: (1) update retry interceptor to skip when request.tag(Boolean)==true or body.contentLength()==-1, (2) add short doc blurb in sampleapp onboarding, (3) add a unit test using MockWebServer to simulate 500 then 200 and verify no duplicate upload exception.

olivia: perfect. thanks. tagging infra/bot to run CI once PR lands.

